 "notes": "Tuteo (tú imperatives: Elige, Pulsa, Mantén pulsado); neutral Spanish usable in Spain and Latin America, avoiding gendered forms for the user (“cuando quieras”, “Todo listo”). Sentence case for titles, buttons and menu items (Guardar cambios, Abrir Ajustes del Sistema); capitalize only proper names and the names of app pages and macOS panes (Ajustes, Modelos, Historial, Ajustes del Sistema, Llavero). Use “ ” quotes, decimal comma and a space before % (10,3 %). Prices as 0,0045 USD. Apple macOS Spanish terminology: Ajustes, Ajustes del Sistema, Llavero, portapapeles, atajo, Atajos, barra de menús, Finder, Dock. Never translated: Airdraft, model/provider names, Apple Intelligence, Apple Speech, Neural Engine, Core ML, keycap names (Control, Option, Command, Shift, Fn, esc, Return), paths, identifiers, URLs. Single-line controls (segments, sidebar footer, table headers) must stay as short as English.",
